' Activity Diagram 04 — IntegerAdd overflow-launder (buggy) vs fail-loudly fix.
'
' A SHARED prefix (the per-deploy diff, deliberately wrapping_sub — the group
' inverse of execution's wrapping add) then splits into two lanes:
'   - BUGGY: combine folds diffs with wrapping_add → the sum wraps to a
'     non-negative value → the apply-time checked_add >= 0 gate is fooled →
'     a laundered wrong value is committed to consensus state (S7).
'   - FIXED: defense-in-depth. (a) combine uses checked_add (None on overflow),
'     (b) cal_merged_result drops the branch, (c) the terminal apply re-checks
'     (checked_add + >=0 -> Err). (d) the diff STAYS wrapping_sub on purpose.
'
' NOTE on node coloring in THIS PlantUML build: the correct form is the suffix
' stereotype  ':label; <<#hex>>'  (verified by rendering; the prefix form is
' deprecated here and emits an in-image warning banner).
'
' Source of truth for the IntegerAdd launder finding in
' docs/casper/theory/finalized-floor/finalized-floor-verification.md (section 6).
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/finalized-floor/diagrams/04-integeradd-launder-and-fix.puml

@startuml 04-integeradd-launder-and-fix
!theme plain

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor        #FFFFFF
  BorderColor            #333333
  ArrowColor             #444444
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
  DiamondBorderColor     #E65100
}
skinparam defaultFontName "monospace"
skinparam defaultFontSize 10
skinparam legendFontName "monospace"
skinparam legendFontSize 10
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam legendBorderColor #666666

title IntegerAdd overflow-launder (buggy) vs fail-loudly checked fix

' Node color legend (suffix <<#hex>> form):
'   amber  (#FFF3E0) = SHARED, correct-and-deliberate diff step
'   red    (#FFEBEE / #FFCDD2 / #EF9A9A) = buggy fold / wrap / launder
'   green  (#C8E6C9 / #A5D6A7)           = fixed gate / safe reject / Err
'   amber diamonds (#FFF8E1)             = overflow decision

start
:per-deploy DIFF  calculate_num_channel_diff\nΔdᵢ = endᵢ − prevᵢ   via wrapping_sub\n(rholang/…/rholang_merging_logic.rs); <<#FFF3E0>>
note right #FFF3E0
  (d) wrapping_sub is DELIBERATE.
  The exact GROUP INVERSE of
  execution's wrapping add —
  see the legend below.
end note

split
  -[#C62828]-> BEFORE the fix;
  partition "BUGGY ── wrapping_add launder asymmetry" #FFEBEE {
    :COMBINE folds diffs Σ Δdᵢ with\nwrapping_add  (SILENT overflow); <<#FFEBEE>>
    :sum WRAPS to a non-negative value\ne.g. i64::MAX + i64::MAX + 2\n≡ 0 (mod 2⁶⁴); <<#FFCDD2>>
    :apply-time  checked_add ≥ 0  gate\nPASSES the wrapped value\n(overflow already hidden upstream); <<#FFCDD2>>
    :laundered WRONG value committed\nto consensus state (safety S7); <<#EF9A9A>>
    kill
  }
split again
  -[#2E7D32]-> AFTER the fix;
  partition "FIXED ── fail-loudly checked (defense-in-depth)" #E8F5E9 {
    :(a) COMBINE  combine_mergeable_value\n(rspace++/…/merging_logic.rs)\nuses checked_add ⟹ None on overflow; <<#C8E6C9>>
    if (combine overflowed? → None) then (yes)
      :(b) cal_merged_result\n(casper/…/conflict_set_merger.rs)\nDROPS the branch (REJECT decision); <<#A5D6A7>>
      kill
    else (no)
      :folded diff in range; <<#C8E6C9>>
    endif
    :(c) TERMINAL APPLY\ncalculate_number_channel_merge\n(rholang/…/rholang_merging_logic.rs)\nchecked_add + ≥ 0 ⟹ Err\n(defense-in-depth backstop —\nthe ACTUAL consensus-state write); <<#A5D6A7>>
    kill
  }
end split

legend bottom
  (d) The DIFF stays wrapping_sub on purpose: it is the exact group inverse of the
  wrapping add that language-level execution used (reduce.rs GInt `+`, intended 64-bit
  semantics), so it faithfully RECOVERS the deploy's true intended delta even when
  execution overflowed. Overflow is caught DOWNSTREAM (combine + apply), NEVER at the
  diff — erroring there would crash live block processing on a deploy that must be
  gracefully merge-rejected.
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Rocq  IntegerAdd.checked_combine_sound (fix is launder-free) · supply_cap_no_launder
  (defense-in-depth bound) · launder_exhibit (the defect is real).
  Z3    integeradd_launder_bitvec.py — BitVec-64 witness vs exact machine i64
  (bvadd == wrapping_add): the launder EXISTS on wrap; checked-combine is launder-free.
  BitmaskOr is unchanged (a semilattice; no overflow lane).
endlegend

@enduml
